course: dictionary
lesson: 9502
title: Family words: stepsister
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A stepsister is a family word, and the clue is in the start of the word, «step». It means the family link came through a parent marrying or partnering someone new, not through birth. A stepsister is the daughter of your stepmother or stepfather, but not the daughter of your own mum or dad.
explain: Here is a clue from the sentence: «A stepbrother or stepsister shares no parent with you; they are the child of your parent's partner.» So if you and a girl share the same mum and dad, she is a sister, not a stepsister. Ask yourself: do we share a parent? If not, she may be a stepsister.
explain: Stories can give a wrong picture. In «Cinderella», the stepsisters are often unkind. Real stepsisters can be kind, and many become good friends. Look at the context: «In Brighton, Theo-Jack draws his family tree at school: two stepsisters, one half-brother, a mum, a stepdad and a dad.»
fact: A stepsister is the daughter of your stepmother or stepfather.
fact: A stepsister does not share a parent with you, because her parent is your parent's partner.
fact: The plural is stepsisters, as in «two stepsisters».
fact: Useful phrases: «my stepsister» and «younger stepsister».
fact: A stepsister can be a good friend, even though stories sometimes show them as unkind.
exercise: What does stepsister mean? | A boy who lives next door | A girl or woman who is your own mum's or dad's daughter by birth | A girl who is your best friend at school | *A girl or woman who is the daughter of your stepmother or stepfather, but not of your own parents
exercise: Look at «two stepsisters, one half-brother, a mum, a stepdad and a dad» in the Brighton sentence. How many stepsisters are on Theo-Jack's family tree? | *Two | One | Three | Four
exercise: Which person shares no parent with you? | A sister born to your mum and dad | A cousin | A twin | *A stepsister, the child of your parent's partner
test: In «Cinderella», the stepsisters are often unkind. What does this show about stories? | *Stories often show stepsisters as unkind, but real stepsisters can be good friends | Stepsisters are always unkind in real life | Stepsisters only live in fairy tales | Stepsisters are always the same age as you
test: When does a girl become your stepsister? | When you are born | *When a parent marries or partners someone who already has a daughter | When your own mum has a baby | When you move to a new school
exam: If you are not sure what stepsister means, what should you do? | Assume it means the same as cousin | *Read the words and sentences around it, then check your meaning still makes sense | Skip it and never come back to it | Guess that it is a type of pet
